{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00444",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.08,
      "end_seconds": 7.48,
      "duration_seconds": 6.4,
      "text": "Doctor, your next patient is here. I've done the basics, I'll read them out in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.41,
      "end_seconds": 11.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "Thank you. Good morning, tell me what's been going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 12.64,
      "end_seconds": 16.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor. I came along to help out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.66,
      "end_seconds": 19.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. We'll go through it together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.19,
      "end_seconds": 32.24,
      "duration_seconds": 11.05,
      "text": "I've been feeling overwhelmed at work. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.69,
      "end_seconds": 34.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "And when did that start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.92,
      "end_seconds": 42.99,
      "duration_seconds": 8.07,
      "text": "For about four days, I'd say. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.39,
      "end_seconds": 45.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "Alright, and how severe is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.85,
      "end_seconds": 57.61,
      "duration_seconds": 10.76,
      "text": "I'd say severe. Oh, and trouble switching off at night. That's been about the same, two weeks. I've been feeling short-tempered too, for three days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.62,
      "end_seconds": 75.67,
      "duration_seconds": 17.05,
      "text": "Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.11,
      "end_seconds": 79.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.68,
      "end_seconds": 83.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Any fainting or weight loss at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.21,
      "end_seconds": 85.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "No, none of those."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.38,
      "end_seconds": 91.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any panic attacks or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.25,
      "end_seconds": 96.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Um, uh, no. None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.62,
      "end_seconds": 99.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.39,
      "end_seconds": 105.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "No, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.51,
      "end_seconds": 122.01,
      "duration_seconds": 15.5,
      "text": "What I'm doing here is putting together three things: what you tell me, what I find when I examine you, and what the tests show. None of those alone is enough, which is why we sometimes need to wait for results before being certain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.54,
      "end_seconds": 124.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "I appreciate you explaining that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.25,
      "end_seconds": 127.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.88,
      "end_seconds": 130.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Yes, pollen. I get sneezing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.58,
      "end_seconds": 135.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Let me make a quick note of that before I forget."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.51,
      "end_seconds": 136.21,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.53,
      "end_seconds": 155.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.43,
      "end_seconds": 157.81,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "No operations, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.38,
      "end_seconds": 161.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.81,
      "end_seconds": 168.23,
      "duration_seconds": 5.42,
      "text": "Escitalopram. I take it 10 milligrams, maybe, once a day for the anxiety."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.91,
      "end_seconds": 172.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Did you happen to bring the box or the paperwork?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.38,
      "end_seconds": 181.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "Okay, so no, it's at home. Paracetamol, 500 milligrams, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 182.77,
      "end_seconds": 187.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 250 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.72,
      "end_seconds": 194.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Alright. Did you bring the up-to-date prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.11,
      "end_seconds": 199.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "Um, no, I left it at home."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.26,
      "end_seconds": 201.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.12,
      "text": "What about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.66,
      "end_seconds": 206.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "I have a couple of drinks on the weekend."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.08,
      "end_seconds": 208.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.12,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.27,
      "end_seconds": 212.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "I smoke, yes, around five a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.72,
      "end_seconds": 216.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Is the room warm enough for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.51,
      "end_seconds": 219.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Well, it's perfect, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.23,
      "end_seconds": 224.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 224.97,
      "end_seconds": 241.45,
      "duration_seconds": 16.48,
      "text": "Well, I've had anxiety for two years now. I took the morning off to come in today. Hmm, um, I have acid reflux, for five years. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 245.47,
      "end_seconds": 248.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "Anyone in the family with similar problems or other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 250.06,
      "end_seconds": 251.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "My brother has asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.14,
      "end_seconds": 267.71,
      "duration_seconds": 14.57,
      "text": "I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 268.41,
      "end_seconds": 272.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "Oh, uh, thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 275.92,
      "end_seconds": 284.13,
      "duration_seconds": 8.21,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Pulse 82, respiratory rate 14. Blood pressure 114 over 81, temp 37.0 degrees, SpO2 99 percent on room air."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.92,
      "end_seconds": 307.17,
      "duration_seconds": 22.25,
      "text": "Okay, noted. Putting together what you've described, my working impression is stress-related symptoms. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. I can't rule out an anxiety disorder yet. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've been feeling overwhelmed at work for about four days, severe, and no weight loss or chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 308.74,
      "end_seconds": 312.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "Right, you know, exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.15,
      "end_seconds": 327.72,
      "duration_seconds": 14.57,
      "text": "Just so you know how the rest of the visit will go: I'll finish my notes, we'll agree on the plan, and the front desk will help with anything that needs booking. You shouldn't need to chase anything yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 328.36,
      "end_seconds": 331.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Good, I was wondering how this would go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.28,
      "end_seconds": 340.21,
      "duration_seconds": 6.93,
      "text": "Let's get blood tests, for stress-related symptoms. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 341.1,
      "end_seconds": 343.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Alright. When can I do that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 344.94,
      "end_seconds": 370.51,
      "duration_seconds": 25.57,
      "text": "Talking to someone, even a counsellor, helps more than people expect. Block out proper breaks in the day, and one evening a week that's yours. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle. I'll also refer you to a counsellor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 370.81,
      "end_seconds": 371.51,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 372.68,
      "end_seconds": 380.02,
      "duration_seconds": 7.34,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 380.4,
      "end_seconds": 381.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 382.47,
      "end_seconds": 388.98,
      "duration_seconds": 6.51,
      "text": "If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 389.47,
      "end_seconds": 390.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "Okay, I understand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 391.55,
      "end_seconds": 394.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Please come and see me in four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 394.48,
      "end_seconds": 397.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Okay, so okay, I'll book that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 398.85,
      "end_seconds": 404.65,
      "duration_seconds": 5.8,
      "text": "Before we finish, can you repeat the plan back to me so I know I haven't been confusing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 405.01,
      "end_seconds": 410.09,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "So, uh, I come back in four weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 411.65,
      "end_seconds": 416.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. I think we've covered it. Do you have any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 416.93,
      "end_seconds": 421.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.95,
      "text": "Um, no, I think that's everything. Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ]
}